
Bootstrap: docker
From: ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.12.17
Stage: uv_stage

Bootstrap: docker
From: vllm/vllm-openai:latest-cu130

%files from uv_stage
    # https://docs.astral.sh/uv/guides/integration/docker/#installing-uv
    # copying the binary from the official distroless Docker image
    /uv /bin/
    /uvx /bin/

%post
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    # build-essential, python3-dev needed for numba compilation such as pooled-ppi
    apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        build-essential \
        ca-certificates \
        curl \
        fd-find \
        git \
        less \
        python-is-python3 \
        python3.13 \
        python3.13-dev \
        ripgrep \
        squashfs-tools \
        zstd

    # nodejs v24 is LTS: https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases 
    # install from NodeSource PPA: https://nodesource.com/products/distributions
    curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_24.x | bash -
    apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        nodejs

    # pi auto-downloads rg/fd at startup unless found on PATH;
    # apt's fd-find only installs `fdfind`, so symlink it
    ln -sf /usr/bin/fdfind /usr/local/bin/fd

    # apt-get cleanup
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* && apt-get clean

    # https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/tree/main/packages/coding-agent#quick-start
    npm install -g --ignore-scripts @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent

%test
    rg --version | head -1
    fd --version
    uv --version
    node -v
    npm -v
    pi --version

%runscript
    set -eu
    exec pi "$@"

%labels
    BuildCommand apptainer build --force sandbox.sif sandbox.def

%help
    Run sandboxed ollama/pi on euler with the following features/fixes/kludges:
    - If the llama.cpp model list looks stale/wrong in `/model`, reset the cache with `rm -rf $EU_VIBE_DIR/home/pi-agent`
    - Has %runscript that starts the ollama server & then an interactive shell
    - Uses `portpicker` to pick a random open port for ollama to fix `Error: listen tcp 127.0.0.1:11434: bind: address already in use`
    - Neither %runscipt nor %startscript are executed with `singularity shell`
    - Using `--containall` prevents mounting the current working directory in the container (amongst other things)
    - Does not mount home, ollama-eu shows how to run with minimal mounts/settings
    - Container contains ollama, nodejs
    - pi + packages kept outside of container, installed locally
    - Based on `nvidia/cuda:12.6.0-runtime-ubuntu22.04` as used in AlphaFold3 so known to work on euler
    - Official docker image (ollama/ollama) fails with `Error: something went wrong, please see the ollama server logs for details`

    Issues:
    - If Pi can't connect to ollama (suddenly/anymore), can "fix" with `rm -rf home`
    - Better mount for ~/.cache?
    - Can leave a stray vllm serve process, find & kill with:
        ```
        nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=pid,process_name,used_memory
        kill ..
        ```
